{"header":{"numFound":25690,"maxScore":17.221191,"queryTime":497,"page":1,"pageSize":10},"results":[{"authors":[{"id":null,"fullName":"Haonan Cui","name":"Haonan","surname":"Cui","rank":1,"pid":null}],"openAccessColor":"gold","publiclyFunded":false,"eoscIfGuidelines":null,"type":"publication","language":{"code":"und","label":"Undetermined"},"countries":null,"subjects":[{"subject":{"scheme":"FOS","value":"02 engineering and technology"},"provenance":null},{"subject":{"scheme":"FOS","value":"0210 nano-technology"},"provenance":null}],"mainTitle":"Design of Silicon-Based Anode Materials for High Energy Density Li-Ion Batteries","subTitle":null,"descriptions":["<jats:p>Compared to other types of batteries, lithium batteries have an extremely high energy density, which means they can store more energy while maintaining a smaller size and weight. The ideal electrode material must have a high lithium ion capacity to store many lithium ions. In addition, the electrode material must have good electronic conductivity to promote lithium ions' rapid entry and exit. However, traditional carbon materials have limited theoretical specific capacity, and the transmission of lithium-ion batteries in traditional materials is limited, resulting in a significant decrease in capacity. Silicon has a theoretical capacity of up to 4200mAh/g, more than ten times the capacity of commercial graphite negative electrodes. In addition, silicon and lithium can undergo alloying reactions to form Li Si alloys, which helps improve the material's specific capacity. This article first summarizes the advantages of electric vehicles and lithium-ion batteries. Then, the benefits and challenges of using silicon-based materials as negative electrodes for lithium-ion batteries were elaborated in detail, and finally, the prospects of silicon-based materials in lithium-ion battery applications were summarized. This article has reference significance in improving the energy density of lithium-ion batteries.</jats:p>"],"publicationDate":"2024-11-07","publisher":"Darcy & Roy Press Co. Ltd.","embargoEndDate":null,"sources":["Crossref"],"formats":null,"contributors":null,"coverages":null,"bestAccessRight":{"code":"c_abf2","label":"OPEN","scheme":"http://vocabularies.coar-repositories.org/documentation/access_rights/"},"container":{"name":"Highlights in Science, Engineering and Technology","issnPrinted":"2791-0210","issnOnline":null,"issnLinking":null,"ep":"269","iss":null,"sp":"264","vol":"116","edition":null,"conferencePlace":null,"conferenceDate":null},"documentationUrls":null,"codeRepositoryUrl":null,"programmingLanguage":null,"contactPeople":null,"contactGroups":null,"tools":null,"size":null,"version":null,"geoLocations":null,"id":"doi_________::01395ae4ec256ba82d949a45c38d1938","originalIds":["10.54097/yr3my387","50|doiboost____|01395ae4ec256ba82d949a45c38d1938"],"pids":[{"scheme":"doi","value":"10.54097/yr3my387"}],"dateOfCollection":null,"lastUpdateTimeStamp":null,"indicators":{"citationImpact":{"citationCount":0.0,"influence":2.1746283E-9,"popularity":1.944044E-9,"impulse":0.0,"citationClass":"C5","influenceClass":"C5","impulseClass":"C5","popularityClass":"C5"}},"projects":null,"organizations":null,"communities":null,"collectedFrom":[{"key":"openaire____::081b82f96300b6a6e3d282bad31cb6e2","value":"Crossref"}],"instances":[{"pids":[{"scheme":"doi","value":"10.54097/yr3my387"}],"license":"CC BY NC","accessRight":{"code":"c_abf2","label":"OPEN","scheme":"http://vocabularies.coar-repositories.org/documentation/access_rights/","openAccessRoute":"hybrid"},"type":"Article","urls":["https://doi.org/10.54097/yr3my387"],"publicationDate":"2024-11-07","refereed":"peerReviewed","hostedBy":{"key":"issn___print::959d637477fafc5f7d297b75638d3d92","value":"Highlights in Science Engineering and Technology"},"collectedFrom":{"key":"openaire____::081b82f96300b6a6e3d282bad31cb6e2","value":"Crossref"}}],"links":null,"otherTitles":null,"inDiamondJournal":false,"green":false,"isGreen":false,"isInDiamondJournal":false},{"authors":[{"id":null,"fullName":"Kai Chen","name":"Kai","surname":"Chen","rank":1,"pid":null},{"id":null,"fullName":"Dian Zhang","name":"Dian","surname":"Zhang","rank":2,"pid":null},{"id":null,"fullName":"Xin Shen","name":"Xin","surname":"Shen","rank":3,"pid":null},{"id":null,"fullName":"Xuning Feng","name":"Xuning","surname":"Feng","rank":4,"pid":null},{"id":null,"fullName":"Xin‐Bing Cheng","name":"Xin‐Bing","surname":"Cheng","rank":5,"pid":{"id":{"scheme":"orcid_pending","value":"0000-0001-7567-1210"},"provenance":null}},{"id":null,"fullName":"Yuping Wu","name":"Yuping","surname":"Wu","rank":6,"pid":null}],"openAccessColor":null,"publiclyFunded":false,"eoscIfGuidelines":null,"type":"publication","language":{"code":"eng","label":"English"},"countries":null,"subjects":[{"subject":{"scheme":"FOS","value":"0211 other engineering and technologies"},"provenance":null},{"subject":{"scheme":"FOS","value":"02 engineering and technology"},"provenance":null}],"mainTitle":"Emerging Thermal Safety Characteristics of Large‐Capacity Lithium Iron Phosphate Lithium‐Ion Batteries","subTitle":null,"descriptions":["<jats:title>Abstract</jats:title>                   <jats:p>Lithium iron phosphate is generally considered to be one of the most thermally stable cathode materials for commercial lithium‐ion batteries, while emerging thermal safety characteristics rise with the large‐capacity lithium‐ion batteries in large‐scale stationary energy storage power stations. In this review, different safety risks of lithium iron phosphate batteries compared with lithium nickel manganese cobalt oxide batteries from the view of general features of thermal runaway and the content of extremely dangerous hydrogen are discussed, especially the emerging thermal safety characteristics for large‐capacity lithium‐ion batteries. First, the prevailing belief that lithium iron phosphate is safer than lithium nickel manganese cobalt oxide is discussed based on the general features of thermal runaway, including characteristic temperature, heat generation, mass loss, and combustion possibility. Second, the rising viewpoint that the hydrogen content in the thermal runaway of lithium iron phosphate batteries is higher than that of lithium nickel manganese cobalt oxide batteries is examined. More importantly, different thermal behaviors are strongly related to the battery capacity (ampere hour). Additionally, the solutions to reduce hydrogen generation in lithium‐ion batteries are presented in the outlook. This review presents comprehensive insights into the thermal safety behaviors of the commercial lithium‐ion batteries with lithium iron phosphate cathodes.</jats:p>"],"publicationDate":"2025-09-22","publisher":"Wiley","embargoEndDate":null,"sources":["Crossref"],"formats":null,"contributors":null,"coverages":null,"bestAccessRight":{"code":"c_14cb","label":"CLOSED","scheme":"http://vocabularies.coar-repositories.org/documentation/access_rights/"},"container":{"name":"Advanced Energy Materials","issnPrinted":"1614-6832","issnOnline":"1614-6840","issnLinking":null,"ep":null,"iss":null,"sp":null,"vol":"16","edition":null,"conferencePlace":null,"conferenceDate":null},"documentationUrls":null,"codeRepositoryUrl":null,"programmingLanguage":null,"contactPeople":null,"contactGroups":null,"tools":null,"size":null,"version":null,"geoLocations":null,"id":"doi_________::ae193a2fac1c826550e72680a0822338","originalIds":["10.1002/aenm.202503248","50|doiboost____|ae193a2fac1c826550e72680a0822338"],"pids":[{"scheme":"doi","value":"10.1002/aenm.202503248"}],"dateOfCollection":null,"lastUpdateTimeStamp":null,"indicators":{"citationImpact":{"citationCount":15.0,"influence":2.825725E-9,"popularity":1.1972337E-8,"impulse":15.0,"citationClass":"C4","influenceClass":"C4","impulseClass":"C4","popularityClass":"C4"}},"projects":null,"organizations":[{"legalName":"Tsinghua University","acronym":"THU","id":"openorgs____::343e897b3a9e6f6facaf57aec940ed2a","pids":[{"sche